1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * 1930 - Sherman Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota.  (age 6)
2 CONT * 1940 - Sherman Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Justin Thomas Thompson, 92, Antler, North Dakota, died Friday, June 3, 2016, at a hospital in Minot, North Dakota..
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born March 16, 1924, on the family farm in Sherman Township, Bottineau County, a son of Sofus and Selma (Feland) Thompson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sofus changed his last name from Drangsholt to Thompson because no one could pronounce Drangsholt.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Justin was raised on the family farm and attended the Sherman Township School. Justin assisted his father farm the land on the Erik Ramstad farm. He had many pleasant memories of Erik and Louise Ramstad and their generosity. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Justin met Phyllis Peterson in 1947 when she came to teach at the Sherman Township School. They were married October 15, 1950, at First Lutheran Church, Minot, North Dakota.  Justin farmed and ranched for many years near 
2 CONT Antler, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT Justin was a member of Bethel Lutheran Brethren Church, Antler, North Dakota.   He was very active in the church and loved the Lord. He was an Elder and chairman of the congregation for over 50 years. He served on the board of the
2 CONC  Mohall Credit Union for 30 years, the Farm Bureau board and the local election board. He loved his Norwegian heritage and loved spending time with his grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family: wife of 65 years, Phyllis Thompson, Antler, North Dakota;  daughters, Janell (Thompson) Power, Minot, North Dakota;  Christine (Steve) Lauer, Antler, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT And grandchildren, Andrea (Donovan) Darling, Bismarck, North Dakota;  Michael Power, Minot, North Dakota; 
2 CONT Jennifer (Lars) Coleman, Lynnwood, Washington;   Angela (Charles) Strand, Minot, North Dakota;  Matthew (Gwendoline) Lauer, Antler, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also great-grandchildren, Zachary Justin Darling, Allison Darling, Emily Coleman, Lucas Coleman, Brynn Strand, Miraya Strand, Charlee Marie Strand, Lochlyn Lauer and Taelyn Lauer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Justin is also survived by sisters, Verdine (Newman) Jelleberg, Bottineau, North Dakota;  Sylvia (Virgil) Christenson, Nevada;   Arlys (Gary) Mathis, Gonvick, Minnesota;  Twylah Larson, Fargo, North Dakota;  brother, Gabe (Donna) 
2 CONC Thompson, Antler; North Dakota;  brother-in-law, Richard Pederson, Minot; North Dakota;  and numerous nieces, nephews and cousins.
2 CONT
2 CONT Justin was preceded in death by his parents; sisters, Inez Thompson, Swanhild Morrison and Marlene Pederson; brothers-in-law, Herbert Newman and Ernest Jelleberg; and nephews, Brian Pederson, Kevin Pederson and Michael Morrison.
2 CONT ----
