1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * 1940 - Sherman Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota. (age 8)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabriel Sofus Thompson, 88, Antler, North Dakota died Tuesday, Dec. 17, 2019, at a hospital in Minot, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born Nov. 10, 1931, on the family farm in Sherman Township, Bottineau County, to Sofus and Selma (Feland) Thompson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was raised on the family farm and attended grade school at the Sherman Township School. He graduated from Antler High School in 1949.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabriel entered the U.S. Army on April 8, 1953. He served as a Corporal with the Signal Corps. He was honorably discharged April 7, 1955.
2 CONT
2 CONT While in the service, Gabriel was united in marriage to Donna Kissner on July 30, 1953, in Fort Marmouth, New Jersey. They moved to White Sands, New Mexico, where he was stationed tracking missiles.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his military service, they moved back to Antler, North Dakota, to the family farm. He farmed and ranched in Wheaton Township where he purchased land and rented other land. They returned to the Sherman Township homestead in 1
2 CONC 974. Although he was retired, he farmed and ranched right up until the end.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabriel was a member of the Bethel Lutheran Brethren Church, Antler, North Dakota, and the George T. Taylor American Legion Post #52, Mohall, North Dakota. He served on the Antler Coop Elevator Board and the Bottineau County Socia
2 CONC l Services Board, and previously served as a Boy Scout troop leader. He enjoyed fishing, hunting and attending the sporting events of his grandchildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He enjoyed helping Donna with their gardens, and the most common phrase on the Thompson Farm if something broke, “Well, Grandpa can fix it.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Family: wife of 66 years, Donna Thompson, Antler, North Dakota;  son, Gabriel (Tracie) Thompson Jr., Antler, North Dakota;  daughter, Kimberly Thompson, Minot and Antler, North Dakota;  son-in-law, James Kammert, Rapid City, South
2 CONC  Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT And grandchildren, Wyatt (Allison) and Talon (Alexis Heinle) Thompson, Colten (Taylor Best) Haider, Jamie Thompson, Katie and Alan Kammert; 
2 CONT
2 CONT He is also survived by his sisters, Verdine (Newman) Jelleberg, Bottineau, North Dakota;  Sylvia (Virgil) Christianson, Carson City, Nevada;  Arlys (Gary) Mathis, Gonvick, Minnesota; and  Twylah Larson, Fargo, North Dakota;  broth
2 CONC ers-in-law, Richard Pederson, Minot, North Dakota; and Terry (Janet) Kissner, Westhope, North Dakota,  and numerous nieces, nephews and cousins.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gabriel was preceded in death by: his parents, Sofus and Selma Thompson; daughter, Valorie Kammert; brother, Justin Thompson; sisters, Inez Thompson, Swanhild Morrison, Marlene Pederson; brothers-in-law, Herbert Newman and Ernest 
2 CONC Jelleberg; nephews, Brian and Kevin Pederson, Michael Morrison; sisters-in-law, Darlene Elven, Shirley Kissner and Jean Kissner; brothers-in-law, Lyle, Verland and Leonard Kissner.
2 CONT ----
