1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * 1920 - Sherman Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota
2 CONT * 1930 - Sherman Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota
2 CONT * 1940 - Sherman Township, Bottineau County, North Dakota
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Minnie Marie Nelson, '''107''', Antler, North Dakota, died Sunday, Oct. 22, 2017, at the Good Samaritan Society, Mohall, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT Minnie was born on March 28, 1910, to Gabriel and Minnie Marie (Gunderson) Feland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She attended Sherman School and helped out on the farm with milking, harvest, gardening and loved her beautiful flowers. At the age of 16 years, she went to Grand Forks to attend Bible School (Hillcrest Lutheran Academy) for one y
2 CONC ear. She had many fond memories of those days and also traveling with the string band in which she played her auto harp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Minnie met Albert Peter Nelson, from Minnesota, who was here in the area building roads. They married on Nov. 10, 1931 and she even made her own wedding cake. They made their home on the Feland farmstead and Albert later bought so
2 CONC me land and built a new house for them to live in. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Later, Minnie’s mother came to live with them and she talked of the good memories they made of cooking, gardening and picking raspberries together. They had no children of their own but she took care of several of her nieces and n
2 CONC ephews and loved them like her own. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a charter member of Bethel Lutheran Brethren Church, rural Antler, North Dakota, and taught Sunday school for many years and was active in the Willing Workers and other ministries of Bethel. Her father, Gabriel, was instru
2 CONC mental in starting this church here in Antler, North Dakota in 1903. She also loved to entertain guests and always invited people into her home to have a meal or stay the night. She talked of having many missionaries, pastors and 
2 CONC even professors from the Synod stay at her house. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband, Albert, passed away on April 4, 1989, and she continued to live on the farm until 2005. At that time she fell and broke her arm and decided to be a resident at the Good Samaritan Home in Mohall, on Oct. 20, 2005.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family: nieces and nephews, Phyllis Thompson, Verdine Newman Jelleberg, Gabriel and Donna Thompson, Richard Pederson, Sylvia and Virgil Christenson, LaVonne and Gary Mathis, Twylah Larson, Margit and Hilary McNallan, Eleanor and L
2 CONC eonard Harris, Gaylord Larson, Arlene and Richard Schelling, Elaine Feland, Marlene Feland, Gloria Aho, Darlene & Dave Aliff, Patricia Kuhl, Marlene and Arlyn Jacobus, Lorrayne Ribe and Diane Jacobus, Phyllis Zimmerman, Gale and D
2 CONC onna Feland, several great-nephews and great-nieces and cousins.
2 CONT
2 CONT Minnie was preceded in death by: her parents; husband; sisters, Selma Thompson, Gilma Larson and Olga Ribe; brothers, Enoch Feland, Art Feland, Edwin Feland, Gilbert Feland, Philip Feland and baby Filip; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also preceded in death by nephews, Justin Thompson, Harold Morrison, Ernie Jelleberg, Herb Newman, Gabriel Feland, Ronnie Feland, Melvin Aho, Duane Zimmerman; nieces, Swannie Morrison, Inez Thompson, Marlene Pederson, Beverly Hame
2 CONC l, Jeanette Larson, Lucinda Greathouse, Joyce Enger and Geraldine Himle.
2 CONT ----
