1 OCCU register nurse
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Janell Justine Power, 69, Minot, North Dakota, formerly of Antler, North Dakota, went to be with Jesus on Thursday, August, 5, 2021, at a Minot, North Dakota hospital, with her family by her side.  Burial at Bethel
2 CONC  Lutheran Brethren Church Cemetery, rural Antler, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT Janell was born December 16, 1951, at Trinity Hospital in Minot, North Dakota to Justin and Phyllis (Peterson) Thompson.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She was raised on the family farm in Antler, North Dakota, attended Antler Public School and graduated from Hillcrest Lutheran Academy in Fergus Falls, Minnesota.  She recently attended and celebrated her 50th high school class re
2 CONC union. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She graduated from Trinity School of Nursing and worked as a register nurse for 37 years.  She was a very kind and compassionate nurse.  Our family was blessed with caring nurses, just like her, during her care on the very floor o
2 CONC n which she worked. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Janell was married in 1977.  She was blessed with a daughter, Andrea, in 1979; and a son, Michael, in 1984.  She attended Bethel Lutheran Brethren Church, Antler, and Our Redeemer’s Lutheran Brethren Church, Minot.  She was involv
2 CONC ed in the church, brought her children up in Our Redeemer’s Church.  She taught and nurtured her faith in the Lord with her family and others. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She loved going to the farm to spend time with her sister, Chris, and brother-in-law, Steve.  She loved getting together with all the family for celebrations, holidays, and just to be together.  She was happy to add daughter-in-la
2 CONC w, Megan, in 2017.  Janell has four grandchildren she loved dearly, Zachary Darling in 2005, Allison Darling in 2009, Juniper Power in 2018, and Ezra Power in 2021. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 2018, she moved into a new condo in Minot, North Dakota, where she loved planting and growing her raised garden of tomatoes and green peppers that her granddaughter, Juniper, liked eating right off the plant.  She also had many
2 CONC  potted flowers that brought color to her patio.  Janell liked MeTV for all her nostalgic shows, her favorites being old westerns.  Janell and Megan liked watching Jeopardy together, trying to guess the answers.  
2 CONT
2 CONT A yearly trip to Medora was always made with daughter, Andrea, and grandkids, Zachary and Allison, with discussions if this year’s musical was better than last’s.  Most recently, she went on a trip with her sister to Minnesota for
2 CONC  a family wedding.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She loved her family so much, and was always there for them, teaching them her kindness for all and her love for Christ.  He used her to show them His perfect, unconditional love for all.  She is very missed and is with our Lord a
2 CONC nd Savior, healed of all our earthly pain and sin.  Thank you Jesus for the amazing woman you placed in our lives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family:  daughter, Andrea Darling, Bismarck, North Dakota; son, Michael (Megan) Power, Minot, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT And grandchildren, Zachary and Allison Darling, and Juniper and Ezra Power; 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is also survived by her sister, Chris (Steve) Lauer, Antler, North Dakota;  nieces, Jennifer (Lars) Coleman, Snohomish, Washington; and Angela (Charles) Strand, Antler, North Dakota;  nephew, Matthew (Gwendoline) Lauer, Antler
2 CONC , North Dakota; many great-nieces, great-nephews, aunts, uncles and cousins.
2 CONT
2 CONT Janell was preceded in death by:  her parents, Justin and Phyllis Thompson; and several aunts and uncles. 
2 CONT ----
